<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table A1: </span>Reliability and sufficiency evaluation results of visual components on <span id="A1.T1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">V*</span> Bench and HR-Bench of the ablation models under different reward schemes: (1) Naive, consisting only of accuracy and format rewards; (2) Curiosity, the curiosity-driven reward scheme proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al. (2025a)</a></cite>; (3) SCCM, our proposed SCCM scheme with visual information sufficiency and minimality constraint; (4) SCCM w/o Minimality, an ablation variant of SCCM without the minimality constraint. We note that <em id="A1.T1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SCCM w/o Minimality</em> (denoted *), is not comparable, as its cropped image is excessively large, being the same size as the original input image.</figcaption>
</figure>
